Subject: [PATCH] phy: qcom: qmp-pcie-msm8996: add the downstream PHY v3 tables

The SM-T825 QCA6174 on RC0 never trained (LTSSM in Polling.Compliance)
with the mainline tables, although the chip runs: its Bluetooth half
answers on UART. Downstream msm_pcie programs PHY version 3 there
(qcom,pcie-phy-ver = <3> in the stock DT): CLK_SELECT 0x35, spread
spectrum off, RX_EQU_ADAPTOR_CNTRL4 0xff, SIGDET_LVL 0x1a and
LP_WAKEUP_DLY_TIME_AUXCLK 0x04.

Add those tables behind a "qcom,msm8996-v3-qmp-pcie-phy" compatible
that falls back to "qcom,msm8996-qmp-pcie-phy", so only boards that ask
for them change. The former 0017 changed the shared tables for every
MSM8996 board.

--- a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/phy/qcom,msm8996-qmp-pcie-phy.yaml
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/phy/qcom,msm8996-qmp-pcie-phy.yaml
@@ -15,7 +15,11 @@
 
 properties:
   compatible:
-    const: qcom,msm8996-qmp-pcie-phy
+    oneOf:
+      - const: qcom,msm8996-qmp-pcie-phy
+      - items:
+          - const: qcom,msm8996-v3-qmp-pcie-phy
+          - const: qcom,msm8996-qmp-pcie-phy
 
   reg:
     items:
--- a/drivers/phy/qualcomm/phy-qcom-qmp-pcie-msm8996.c
+++ b/drivers/phy/qualcomm/phy-qcom-qmp-pcie-msm8996.c
@@ -136,6 +136,85 @@
 	QMP_PHY_INIT_CFG(QPHY_V2_PCS_TXDEEMPH_M3P5DB_V0, 0x0e),
 };
 
+/*
